From 592c243e1e05c00d3238ce75727c4d98be7989a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew <matthewhale@live.com.au>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:57:06 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 53/59] game.xvt_components: X-Wing vs TIE Fighter starship
 components

1998 flight, every craft but starfighters. The OPT mesh descriptors decide
everything, as in XvT: meshes with explosion flag 2 get XvT's hit points for
their type (g_meshTypeComponentMaxHp) and stay drawn (X-Wing hides every
starship's turrets but the corvette's); hits on meshes with flag 1 go to the
component first once both shield banks are empty (Craft_DamageComponent's
16-point units, remainder to the hull), except shield generators, which take
hits through the shields as X-Wing's ISD generators do. A destroyed turret or
gun stops the turret slots nearest it (X-Wing's hardpoints have no mesh index;
this reproduces X-Wing's corvette mapping), and the last shield generator
takes the shields and shield system with it, as on X-Wing's ISD.

The player targets components with , and Shift+, (XvT's selectable-mesh
rule, nearest hull section on a new target, next one when it is destroyed).
A starship's targeted component is boxed on the HUD, ranges the CMD and the
warhead lock, and player warheads home on it. The CMD names it (XvT CMD:
in place of "Hull"). Game page: Starship Components.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
